ma, developed by Aleister Crowley, created a distinct spiritual framework that the OTO adopted and propagated globally."}, {"sourceSlug": "austin-osman-sparke", "sourceName": "Austin Osman Spare", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "ordo-templi-orientis", "targetName": "Ordo Templi Orientis", "context": "Austin Osman Spare collaborated with the OTO in the early 20th century, contributing to its artistic and esoteric developments."}], "places": [{"name": "Vienna, Austria", "role": "Birthplace"}, {"name": "San Francisco, USA", "role": "Major Lodge"}, {"name": "Paris, France", "role": "Cultural Hub"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Ordo Templi Orientis", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "ordo-templi-orientis"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q33237", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ordo_Templi_Orientis"], "tags": ["religious organization", "Religious Institutions", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Ordo Templi Orientis contributed to the historical record of the Modern period. Key lasting impacts include: Shaped institutional landscape and community development. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "The OTO significantly shaped modern occultism and alternative spiritual movements, influencing diverse cultural expressions and fostering community among practitioners since its founding. Its teachings have resonated with millions, particularly during the countercultural shifts of the 20th century.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-06-29T10:08:29Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#28364274155", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "International fraternal and religious organization Founded 1903.", "newValue": "The Ordo Templi Orientis (OTO) emerged in the early 20th century as a pivotal fraternal and religious organization, founded in 1903 by Carl Kellner in Vienna, Austria. It became significant for its unique synthesis of Western esotericism and ceremonial magic, heavily influenced by the writings of Aleister Crowley, who assumed leadership in 1912. The OTO's global reach and eclectic teachings have made it a notable entity in the history of modern occultism, intertwining personal spiritual exploration with broader cultural movements in the realms of mysticism and countercultural philosophy.

The organization expanded rapidly during the 20th century, establishing branches across Europe and the Americas. Key events included the introduction of Crowley's Thelema philosophy, which emphasized individual will and the pursuit of one's true path. The OTO also played a crucial role in the revival of interest in esoteric traditions, influencing various artistic and intellectual movements. It hosted numerous public rituals and events that attracted a diverse membership, from artists to intellectuals, and contributed to the flourishing of alternative spiritual practices in the post-war era.

